   "question": "How has parliament discussed Closing the Gap outcomes?",
   "answer": "Based on the provided context, Parliament discussed the life expectancy gap between Indigenous and non-Indigenous Australians through a question to the Minister representing the Minister for Immigration and Multicultural and Indigenous Affairs. The question noted that Australia\u2019s performance in closing this gap is \u201cthe worst in the Western world,\u201d cited the Fred Hollows Foundation\u2019s view that Australia had fallen behind comparable countries, and asked why Indigenous life expectancy is 15 to 20 years less, compared with smaller gaps in New Zealand, Canada, and the United States.\n\nParliament also discussed related Indigenous reconciliation and recognition matters, including a motion and remarks about Indigenous Australians being \u201cvisibly and actively part of our national life.\u201d",
